{
  "id": "Compound::DB08820 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Ivacaftor is classified as a Cytochrome P450 3a (Cyp3a) inhibitor, and its inclusion in this category links it to drugs like Darunavir and Lopinavir, both of which bind to Cyp3a4. The shared ancestry of Ivacaftor and these drugs, through the lowest common ancestor Carboxamide, suggests a potential mechanism by which Ivacaftor may influence Cyp3a4 activity. The evidence from the paths highlights a recurring relationship where drugs in the Cyp3a inhibitor class bind to Cyp3a4, and Ivacaftor, as a member of this class, may exert a similar effect. The final scores from the paths indicate a consistent level of confidence in this relationship, reinforcing the idea that Ivacaftor could act as a modulator of Cyp3a4 function. The integration of these paths suggests a plausible mechanism where Ivacaftor, through its classification and binding interactions, may influence Cyp3a4 activity, potentially affecting drug metabolism.",
